+/* VKD3D fex35 (fex_ui_split.c, VKD3D_FEX_UI_SPLIT): FEX's frame generation layer gets each frame twice, as shown and
+ * without the game's UI layer, so it can make the frames in between from the scene alone and lay the real frame's UI
+ * on top. D2R draws its UI (map overlay, HUD, labels) into a back-buffer-sized RGBA16F image that starts with a clear,
+ * then mixes it into the back buffer with one 3-vertex draw. Before that draw, the back buffer goes into a copy of its
+ * own (vkd3d_fex_ui_frame); if the draw doesn't blend over the back buffer, it is drawn again into that copy with the
+ * UI layer cleared (the UI layer is saved before and put back after). Each swapchain blit then copies that frame, or
+ * the back buffer itself when no copy was made since the last Present(), into one image the layer finds by how it is
+ * made (vkd3d_fex_ui_out_image_info()). */
